WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Look at Queen Victoria's
family across four generations.

2
00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.730
A disorder in which blood clots
slowly turns up again and again.

3
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.510
Her son Leopold had it.

4
00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.960
So did grandsons, and great-grandsons.

5
00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:17.660
In this family tree, every
affected person is male.

6
00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:19.760
Not one daughter had it.

7
00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:25.460
So why do some inherited conditions turn up
far more often in sons than in daughters?

8
00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:29.040
In this mission, you'll learn to
read a family tree like this one,

9
00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.920
symbol by symbol.

10
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:35.320
Then you'll find out which parent's cell
decides whether a child is a son or a

11
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.420
daughter.

12
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:41.200
Your mission: explain why some inherited
conditions turn up far more often in

13
00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.030
sons.
